cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (12.855-Octave, 0.0905-670.69 um) Space-Lyman to SOFIA/Herschel THz, ISO SWS, HST STIS E140H, JWST, Coherent Jerk-Drift, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space Lyman-limit/FUV/NUV (FUSE 0.0905-0.1187 um, HST/COS G130M
  0.1125-0.1450 um, HST/STIS E140H R=114,000 FUV, HST/STIS E140M 0.1145-0.1710 um,
  HST/STIS E230M/E230H 0.1605-0.3150 um), ground near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV), optical (HARPS,
  HARPS-N, ESPRESSO HR/UHR, Gemini GHOST BLUE+RED with simultaneous sky-IFU veto, Gemini
  GRACES, Euler CORALIE, OHP SOPHIE, OHP ELODIE, CFHT ESPaDOnS, MPG/ESO FEROS, VLT
  FLAMES/GIRAFFE HR), far-red (VLT UVES_RED, CARMENES_VIS with SERVAL RV alignment), 3-arm
  simultaneous UVB+VIS+NIR (VLT X-shooter 0.2989-2.4790 um), near-infrared YJH (NIRPS_HE),
  thermal J/H/K (VLT CRIRES+), SDSS APOGEE-2 H-band (up to N=28 visits), simultaneous YJHK
  (CFHT SPIRou APERO 0.7.295), JWST space optical-to-thermal-IR (NIRISS SOSS, NIRSpec
  G140H/G235H/G395H, MIRI LRS/MRS), continuous ISO SWS (2.36-45.39 um), airborne IR
  (SOFIA EXES 5.62-26.13 um, R~86,000; SOFIA FORCAST 4-grism G063/G111/G227/G329),
  Spitzer IRS SL+LL (5.20-37.86356 um), Herschel far-IR/THz (PACS 51-210 um, SPIRE FTS
  194-670.69 um, HIFI 0.56-1.16 THz at R=2.2e6), and SOFIA GREAT super-THz heterodyne
  (1.2-4.7 THz, up to R=1.94e7) laser, 30-campaign cubic-jerk/periodic coherent shift-stack
  drift (DRIFT_V56 across 30 N>=4 campaigns / 38,226 trajectories / 2.299B pixel integrals),
  greenhouse CCF, Dyson waste-heat vs. silicate-belt discrimination, and periodic
  frequency-comb technosignatures (0.0905-670.69081 um, 12.855 unbroken octaves across
  33 spectrographs / 51 arms; 473 unique stars and 2,700 archival exposures totaling
  921.5744 h across V3.0-V5.6 + COMB_V4_1 with Keplerian planetary de-Doppler across
  143 orbital campaigns, 41,973 synthetic calibration trials, 423,988 Legacy V2 false
  alarms eliminated, deterministic Stage-2 physical triage, and uniform all-sky COMB_V4_1
  filtering across 458 stacks), unified with 1.4 GHz Parkes/GBT radio searches and TESS
  photometry achieving 23/23 (100%) radio-echelle closure across a 473-system synthesis
  (0 verified ETI detections; 0.0973 W HST_STIS Proxima Cen, 0.065460 kW HST_STIS_E140H
  Alpha Cen A, 0.039712 kW JWST_NIRISS_SOSS SIMP 0136, 0.455538 kW CARMENES_VIS GJ 1286,
  2,781.39 kW ISO_SWS HD 219134, 70.703128 kW HERSCHEL_SPIRE_FTS AB Aur, 19,268,981 kW
  SOFIA_GREAT HD 141569, 21,388,409 kW SOFIA_FORCAST HD 166191, 235,044.17 kW HERSCHEL_HIFI
  R Dor, 66 calibrated panchromatic bridges across 780 cells [68 multi-phase targets]
  alongside 173 <10 pc stars with 1.4558 kW median limit).
